Z||000004||Oreif||03-03-2001||12:35 PM||||Rodney Dickman sells a replacement speaker for the factory sub. From what I've heard it sounds a lot better than the stock one.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||03-03-2001||12:47 PM||||Thanks Oreif, It'll sound better than this one for sure, I,ll check it out.  I knew the Five inch speaker was hard to come by. I have yet to hear the factory sub system working properly in a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||03-03-2001||04:23 PM||||LZeitgeist has the Performance Sound in his 88 Formula.  It sounds pretty good.  It's really more of a mid-bass driver than a sub, but it adds some good presence to the sound.  At least as good as the entry level sound systems in modern cars.  Not quite up to the Monsoon quality (no where near, actually) but good for the time.  He also added a factory Delco AM/FM CD player so the complete install looks totally factory.  It's really sweet!  He even changed the display on the radio to match the red dash lights.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_Freak||03-05-2001||09:14 AM||||Yeah...I have an 8" sub in a round sealed box that tucks into the passenger floorboard, but I bought Rodney's speaker because I wanted to footwell back.  It better than the original factory sub, but if there's any other way I can squeeze those 10"s in like Fierosound I think I'm going to to that... It's too much of a difference from my TA with two 15"s to the 5" midbass.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||03-05-2001||03:35 PM||||Coy,<P>I did my own speaker rebuild and it worked out great. The cone on mine was goo but the foam was roten. What I did was buy a $9.00 speaker from Wal-Mart and remove the foam seal. I then used rubber contact cement and glued it onto the sub-woofer speaker cone and frame. It's been working well for almost six months now. If you want details, try a search on in this section.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy||||reg||14
Z||000009||GarethWright||03-05-2001||06:36 PM||||I just replaced the speaker in the factory sub box with a 6" Focal Utopia. I replaced the metal speaker mount with a wooden cut-out I made.  I have yet to seal it with silicone and remount the grill but it sounds great right now.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Wolfhound||03-05-2001||08:27 PM||||Roy, Same with mine. Cone is OK. I,ll give that a shot. Thanks!!<P>Found your instructions, Great!<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Wolfhound||03-06-2001||03:52 PM||||Roy something like this!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/subfix.JPG">  <BR>No luck at Kmart but Radio Shack had a 5" 8 ohm that I canibalized. Using a chisel end X-acto blade I managed to get all of the foam baffle off intact. Worked perfect. Guess to be on the safe side, I,ll wait until tommorow to try it. <BR>Thanks Coy<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfixit58||03-07-2001||07:40 AM||||Exactly! It's amazing how simple it is, isn't it.<P>Let me know what you think of the sound.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000013||Wolfhound||03-08-2001||06:01 AM||||Well, I put the speaker back in and had some kind of overall buzzing. Checked all conections and realised some ijit hadn't put his antenna back on after swaping fenders.<BR>Replaced antenna and it sounds great. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||stsmithgt||03-08-2001||02:35 PM||||I've tried that same speaker from radio shack.  The buzzing you here (or at least that I'm experiencing) could be the cone or rim of the cone bouncing off the speaker grill.  That speaker has a lot of movement.  Testing it outside of the box there's no buzzing.  Inside the box, buzzing.  I shimmed mine up an eight of and inch tuesday and it still buzzes.  I need to double check for any other reason it would buzz while installed in that funky box.  Maybe that bracket the speaker is mounted to torques on it to make the coil buzz in the speaker.?¿ or not.¡! I tried to go cheap for a temperary fix, but I've put so much time in messing around with it, I should have gone for the gusto and installed the massive WOOF I wanted in the first place.  Good luck finding a solution. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
